  "worked_solution": "The diagonal $\\overset{\u2015}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $\u25b3ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951536/assets/b1d0cf7c5a7c6ad7f0f52c8686239920fabcb05be57372ae0c7c9c9491838a52.png)\n\n Computing the area of $\u25b3ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACB} & =\\frac{1}{2}(10)(6)\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{60}^{\u2218} \\\\  & =30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061{60}^{\u2218} \\\\  & \u224825.981,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 25.981 \\\\  & =51.962.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram is $52.$",
